#conversation file
version=0.1

question "There's a lot of chairs in here." {
    tag=Room_01
    answer=Is there?
    answer=...
    answer=Huh. Yeah.

    question "Sit anywhere." {
        tag=Room_01
        answer=I'll stand here.
        answer=Sorry — do you want me to start?

        question "Say your name." {
            tag=Room_01
            answer=Alex. I'm twenty-eight.
            answer=I don't really know what else you want. I've never done anything.

            question "You're here about someone." {
                tag=Room_01
                answer=...
                answer=Yeah.
                answer=Do we do that bit now or is there a run-up?

                question "There's a run-up if you want one." {
                    tag=Room_01
                    answer=No. Let's just.
                    answer=His name was Sam. Four years in September.

                    question "Alright. Questions." {
                        id=shared1
                        tag=Room_01
                        answer=Go on.

                        question "How did you meet?" {
                            tag=Room_02
                            answer=Nothing story. Someone's kitchen at a party neither of us wanted to be at.
                            answer=And still we met… a sea of people and still we met.

                            question "You've said that before." {
                                tag=Room_02
                                answer=Every day for four years, in my head.
                                answer=It's the only part I let myself have. The meeting bit.
                                answer=We were parallel lines that found a reason to converge.

                                question "What was he like?" {
                                    tag=Room_02
                                    answer=He could make you feel confident in yourself.
                                    answer=Not by saying anything. He just looked at you like you were already fine and you'd go along with it.
                                    answer=I was so sad back then.. Always so sullen but i met someone who was kind enough to share their happiness with me.

                                    question "Share it how?" {
                                        tag=Room_02
                                        loop_to=shared1
                                        answer=He'd just give it away. He had loads and he never checked what he had left.
                                        answer=I've thought about that a lot since.
                                        answer=I never once asked him if he had enough for himself.
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        question "When did you last see him?" {
                            tag=Room_03
                            answer=A Thursday.
                            answer=You never know when itll be the last time.

                            question "Tell me about it." {
                                tag=Room_03
                                answer=It was nothing. That's what I need you to understand. It was completely nothing.
                                answer=We got chips. He was annoyed about his car. I was on my phone for part of it.
                                answer=He hugged me outside the shop, which he did every time, and I did the thing where you pat someone's back twice to end it.

                                question "You've thought about that pat." {
                                    tag=Room_03
                                    answer=Four years.
                                    answer=Two pats. Like I had somewhere to be.
                                    answer=I didn't have anywhere to be. I went home and watched telly.

                                    question "You couldn't have known." {
                                        tag=Room_03
                                        answer=I know that.
                                        answer=Everyone says it and it's true and it doesn't touch the thing at all.
                                        answer=Someone has to leave first this is a very old story there is no other version of this story.

                                        question "..." {
                                            tag=Room_03
                                            loop_to=shared1
                                            answer=I tell myself that when it's bad. It helps about as much as anything else, which is not much.
                                            answer=Somebody was always going to go first. It was always going to be one of us stood there.
                                            answer=It just wasn't supposed to be at twenty-four.
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        question "What happened to you after?" {
                            tag=Room_04
                            answer=I stopped.
                            answer=Not dramatically. I went to the funeral, I was good at the funeral, everyone said how well I was doing.
                            answer=Then about five months later I stopped.

                            question "Stopped how?" {
                                tag=Room_04
                                answer=Work, phone, door.
                                answer=And there was one night.
                                answer=I'm not doing details. Is that alright.

                                question "That's alright." {
                                    tag=Room_04
                                    answer=Everywhere.
                                    answer=Not just the usual places people do. Everywhere I could reach.
                                    answer=Like I was trying to make the outside match, or make it visible, or — I don't know. I've had four years and I still can't finish that sentence.

                                    question "Did anyone find you?" {
                                        tag=Room_04
                                        answer=Eventually.
                                        answer=My neighbour, weirdly. Not anyone I'd have picked.

                                        question "Where were your friends?" {
                                            tag=Room_04
                                            answer=...
                                            answer=That's the question, isn't it.
                                            answer=They were where I'd left them. They'd all been ringing for months and I'd not picked up, and then they stopped ringing, which is what happens.

                                            question "Do you blame them?" {
                                                tag=Room_04
                                                loop_to=shared1
                                                answer=No.
                                                answer=I want violently and I wait, nothing good has happened because i have willed it.
                                                answer=I've never once asked anyone for anything. Then I'm surprised when it doesn't arrive.
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        question "You're good to people though." {
                            tag=Room_04
                            answer=I'm the person everyone rings.
                            answer=Three in the morning, doesn't matter, I'll get up and drive.
                            answer=I've talked two people through the worst nights of their lives and both of them are still here.

                            question "That's not nothing." {
                                tag=Room_04
                                answer=It's not nothing.
                                answer=It's also — sorry, this'll sound like self-pity and I hate self-pity.

                                question "Say it anyway." {
                                    tag=Room_05
                                    answer=Nobody drives to me.
                                    answer=I've got the number of everyone I've ever helped. Not one of them has my bad nights in their diary.
                                    answer=I'm not owed it. I've never told any of them I have bad nights. So it's my own doing and it's still true.

                                    question "You could tell them." {
                                        tag=Room_05
                                        loop_to=shared1
                                        answer=And be the one who needs something.
                                        answer=I've got exactly one thing left that I'm good at and that's being the one who doesn't.
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        question "Does it get better?" {
                            tag=Room_05
                            answer=Attachment is the root of all misery.

                            question "Do you believe it?" {
                                tag=Room_05
                                answer=I believed it for about two years. I built a whole life out of it.
                                answer=Don't get close, don't get hurt. Very tidy. Very cheap.
                                answer=Then I worked out what it actually meant, which is that the answer to loving somebody is to never do it again.

                                question "And now?" {
                                    tag=Room_05
                                    loop_to=shared1
                                    answer=There will be a piece of him in me always.
                                    answer=The only thing you can do is stop adding people, which is what I've done, and it's not the same as being free.
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        question "That's all I wanted to ask." {
                            tag=Room_05
                            answer=Right.
                            answer=...
                            answer=Can I ask you something. Off the record.

                            question "Go on." {
                                tag=Room_05
                                answer=Is he in it? The film.
                                answer=Because he's not one of your people, he never did anything like this, he was the happy one. He was the happiest person I've ever met.
                                answer=I just want him mentioned somewhere. That's all. I don't need it to be about him.

                                question "He's in it." {
                                    tag=Room_05
                                    ending
                                    ending_text=Alex will drive to anyone. Three in the morning, any distance, no questions.
                                    ending_text=Nobody has their number for that. They have never given it out and they never will, and both of those are choices, and neither of them feels like one.
                                    ending_text=A sea of people, and still they met. Somebody had to leave first. There is no other version of this story.
                                    answer=...
                                    answer=Okay.
                                    answer=Thanks. That's — yeah.
                                    answer=Sam. It's Sam. With an m.
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
